 "epi_stream": {"label": "sub-01", "order": "session label", "reading": "Raw: the raw BIDS series, resampled once (cubic interpolation) onto the grid of the preprocessed series by the session's one rigid placement, that of the anchor run's registration, and nothing else done to it; that resampling smooths single-volume detail slightly and enters the difference. Preprocessed: the series as the pipeline wrote it. Their difference, and how each lies on the white and pial contours, is what this page shows: quality control of the raw data and of the preprocessing.", "memory_mib": 512, "rules": {"chunks": "a chunk holds chunk_volumes volumes (the last one fewer) as residuals: (value - ref) mod 256, ref being ref.bin of the run and stream", "common_scale": "with intensity normalization off, one linear window for the whole stream: 0 to the largest hi of its runs (H); a stored value b of a run with window (0, hi) is shown as floor(b * (hi / H) + 0.5), clipped to 0..255", "difference": "every difference view is raw minus pre of the two stored 8-bit values", "files": "every .bin file is a zlib stream", "frame": "per run, the displacement between its own stored transform and the anchor's over its brain mask (mm); flagged when the maximum exceeds limit_mm", "order": "a volume is nx*ny*nz bytes; voxel (i, j, k) is at i + nx*(j + ny*k)", "quantise": "value = clip(floor((v - lo) * 255 / (hi - lo) + 0.5), 0, 255), float32", "ref": "rounded mean of the 8-bit volumes 0, 10, 20, ...", "sd_window": "per run, both streams: 0 to the 99.5th percentile of the temporal SD of the preprocessed series inside the run's brain mask", "slices": "grids[].slice_mm[plane][k] is the signed distance in mm of slice k's plane from the origin of the anatomy's world, along the unit normal grids[].slice_normal[plane] (RAS, the way k grows); the planes on screen meet in the point x with normal . x = distance for each plane, and on another grid the slice of a plane nearest to x is the one whose distance is nearest normal' . x", "stills": "temporal mean and SD (n - 1) over the volumes that the confounds table does not mark as non-steady-state, in float64, then 8 bit", "stream": "the movie of a subject is its sessions in order and, within a session, its packed runs one after the other in the order of runs[] (acquisition order), one stream; runs[].first is the index of a run's first volume within its session", "value": "a stored value b of a run with window (lo, hi) stands for the signal lo + b * (hi - lo) / 255, the middle of the values that quantise to b ([lo + (b - 0.5) * (hi - lo) / 255, lo + (b + 0.5) * (hi - lo) / 255); b = 0 also holds everything below, b = 255 everything above); the same for the SD stills under sd_window", "window": "per run, both streams: 0 to the 99.5th percentile of the preprocessed series inside the run's brain mask, over the volumes 0, 10, 20, ..."}, "contour_unit": 64, "sessions": [{"session_uid": "1344072c4fca9699", "label": "sub-01 ses-1", "media_url": "/epi-media/f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0/1344072c4fca9699/", "fd_threshold_mm": 0.5, "registration": {"anchor": "b478856e6d1ec7c1", "rule": "acquisition_time", "limit_mm": 10.0, "shared_frame_plausible": false, "anchor_is_outlier": false, "portable_voxel_map": true, "reading": "Raw: the raw BIDS series, resampled once (cubic interpolation) onto the grid of the preprocessed series by the session's one rigid placement, that of the anchor run's registration, and nothing else done to it; that resampling smooths single-volume detail slightly and enters the difference. Preprocessed: the series as the pipeline wrote it. Their difference, and how each lies on the white and pial contours, is what this page shows: quality control of the raw data and of the preprocessing.", "anchor_packed": true, "note": null}, "grids": [{"grid_key": "e2babfc70bbc", "shape": [17, 18, 14], "voxel_mm": [8.0, 8.0, 8.0], "oblique_deg": 0.0, "edge_letters": {"axial": ["R", "L", "A", "P"], "coronal": ["R", "L", "S", "I"], "sagittal": ["P"